'''Kruk's Dungeon''' is a large labyrinth whose entrance is hidden under jungle grass west of [[Marim]] on [[Ape Atoll]].

The dungeon is visited during [[Monkey Madness II]] to kill [[Kruk]] and sabotage [[Glough]]'s laboratory. After completing Monkey Madness II, the laboratory is destroyed and becomes a hunter training area for [[Maniacal monkey (Hunter)|maniacal monkeys]].

The [[dwarf multicannon]] can be used in the dungeon.

{{Map|name=Kruk's Dungeon|x=2715|y=2789|r=2|mtype=square|caption=The entrance to the dungeon.|align=left}}

==Navigating==
The dungeon has multiple layers and numerous paths, which a full guide for navigating can be found [[Monkey_Madness_II#Chapter_II|here]].

This dungeon is unique in that the navigation of it is different for each player, as there are numerous nodes which may be interacted with, but only one of them will work. Players may choose to navigate an obstacle course or run through hordes of both [[Maniacal monkey]]s and [[Maniacal monkey archer]]s to reach the end destination. The lower floor of the dungeon is very [[darkness|dark]], so a [[light source]] is required or the player will rapidly take damage after being in the dark for too long. The lower floor is also a popular spot for players training [[Ranged]] or [[Magic]] through multi-targeting Maniacal monkeys.

[[Greegree]]s can be used only around the [[Monkeybars (Kruk's Dungeon)|monkeybars]], around the exit rope, a part of the room where you fight Kruk, and in Glough's laboratory/hunter training area. The greegree will lose its effectiveness when you enter the cave and "wrench itself from your hands." '''If your inventory is full, the greegree will drop to the ground when you enter.''' 

At the end of the dungeon is where players will fight Kruk to progress through the quest. North of the initial entrance, [[monkeybars (Kruk's Dungeon)|monkeybars]] can be seen and can '''''only''''' be used while the player is holding a [[Kruk monkey greegree]].

==Hunter area==
After the quest, the remains of Glough's laboratory becomes a [[Hunter]] training area. Players must mount a [[stunted demonic gorilla]]s to be able to bait the large boulder [[deadfall trap]]s with [[bananas]] to catch [[Maniacal monkey (Hunter)|maniacal monkeys]].

The area contains numerous bone spawns which can be converted to bananas via the [[Bones to Bananas]] spell.

